{
  "name": "Blog Post Creation -- Outline + Content",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Blog Post Creator\n\n**Two webhooks, one workflow:**\n\n1. `POST /blog-post-outline` — accepts topic, voice, anecdotes, opinions, stats toggle, keywords (focus/header/entities/common/extra), plus optional context blocks (intent from search-intent, salience from salience-brief, audience from question-research). If stats is enabled, scrapes Exa + summarises via Gemini Flash, then generates a markdown outline.\n\n2. `POST /blog-post-content` — accepts the edited outline + the same keyword inputs, expands it into final blog copy.\n\n**Empathy Research:**\nWhen `empathy_enabled` is true in the outline request, the workflow scrapes Reddit, forums, YouTube, and Google PAA for reader pain points, objections, problems, and fears — then clusters them via Gemini Flash into an `<empathy_context>` block the outline LLM uses to shape sections around real audience needs.\n\n**Error handling:**\n- A Workflow Error Trigger catches ANY unhandled node error and returns JSON `{error: ...}` instead of n8n's default HTML error page.\n- This prevents the \"Webhook did not return JSON (HTTP 200)\" frontend error.\n\n**Before running:**\n1. API keys for OpenRouter and Exa are pre-filled in the Code nodes.\n2. Activate the workflow and copy the two Production webhook URLs into the frontend's Blog Post Creation tab.\n3. Both webhook nodes have `allowedOrigins: \"*\"` for CORS.\n\n**Model choices (all swappable):**\n- Stats summarisation: `google/gemini-2.5-flash` (cheap, fast)\n- Outline + content: `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5` (strongest for long-form SEO + structure)",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "sticky-readme",
      "name": "README",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -280
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## API Keys\n\nOpenRouter API key is baked into the Code nodes (Stats Scrape, Build Outline Prompt, Build Content Prompt).\n\nExa API key is baked into the Stats Scrape node.\n\nKeys are pre-filled. To rotate, edit the Code nodes directly.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "sticky-keys",
      "name": "API Keys",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "blog-post-outline",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {
          "allowedOrigins": "*"
        }
      },
      "id": "outline-webhook",
      "name": "Outline Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -500,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "blog-post-outline"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "is-test-cond-outline",
              "leftValue": "={{ !!($json.body?.test || $json.test) }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "outline-is-test",
      "name": "Is Outline Test?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -300,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { \"ok\": true, \"message\": \"Webhook reachable\", \"received_at\": $now.toISO() } }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "outline-respond-test",
      "name": "Respond Outline Test OK",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        -200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Normalize inputs from the blog-post-outline webhook.\nconst input = $input.first().json;\nconst form = (input && typeof input.body === 'object' && input.body !== null && Object.keys(input.body).length > 0)\n  ? input.body\n  : input;\n\nconst norm = s => String(s).toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '');\nconst pick = (...keys) => {\n  for (const k of keys) {\n    if (form[k] !== undefined && form[k] !== null && form[k] !== '') return form[k];\n  }\n  const targets = keys.map(norm);\n  for (const k of Object.keys(form)) {\n    const n = norm(k);\n    if (targets.some(t => n === t || n.startsWith(t))) return form[k];\n  }\n  return '';\n};\n\nconst toArr = v => {\n  if (Array.isArray(v)) return v.map(x => String(x).trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  if (typeof v === 'string') return v.split(/[,;\\n]/).map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  return [];\n};\n\nconst parseBool = v => {\n  if (typeof v === 'boolean') return v;\n  if (typeof v === 'string') return v.toLowerCase() === 'true' || v === '1';\n  if (typeof v === 'number') return v !== 0;\n  return false;\n};\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    topic: pick('topic', 'Topic') || '',\n    voice: pick('voice', 'Voice') || '',\n    anecdotes: pick('anecdotes', 'Anecdotes') || '',\n    opinions: pick('opinions', 'Opinions') || '',\n    stats_enabled: parseBool(pick('stats_enabled', 'Stats Enabled', 'statsEnabled')),\n    empathy_enabled: parseBool(pick('empathy_enabled', 'Empathy Enabled', 'empathyEnabled')),\n    focus_keyword: pick('focus_keyword', 'Focus Keyword', 'focusKeyword') || '',\n    header_keywords: toArr(pick('header_keywords', 'Header Keywords', 'headerKeywords')),\n    entities: toArr(pick('entities', 'Entities')),\n    common_keywords: toArr(pick('common_keywords', 'Common Keywords', 'commonKeywords')),\n    extra_keywords: toArr(pick('extra_keywords', 'Extra Keywords', 'extraKeywords')),\n    target_word_count: parseInt(pick('target_word_count', 'Target Word Count', 'targetWordCount')) || 0,\n    intent_context_text: String(pick('intent_context_text', 'intentContextText') || '').trim(),\n    serp_context_text: String(pick('serp_context_text', 'serpContextText') || '').trim(),\n    salience_context_text: String(pick('salience_context_text', 'salienceContextText') || '').trim(),\n    audience_context_text: String(pick('audience_context_text', 'audienceContextText') || '').trim()\n  }\n}];\n"
      },
      "id": "outline-normalize",
      "name": "Normalize Outline Inputs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -100,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// If stats_enabled, search Exa for statistics/data related to the topic\n// and summarise with Gemini Flash.\n//\n// REPLACE these constants with your real keys:\n//   OPENROUTER_API_KEY\n//   EXA_API_KEY\n\nconst OPENROUTER_API_KEY = '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';\nconst EXA_API_KEY = 'b0beb520-610f-4246-ade5-7620631a89aa';\nconst STATS_MODEL = 'google/gemini-2.5-flash';\n\nconst form = $('Normalize Outline Inputs').first().json;\n\nif (!form.stats_enabled) {\n  return [{\n    json: {\n      stats_enabled: false,\n      stats_block: '',\n      source_count: 0\n    }\n  }];\n}\n\nconst query = (form.topic || form.focus_keyword || '').trim();\nif (!query) {\n  return [{ json: { stats_enabled: true, stats_block: '', source_count: 0, error: 'No topic or focus keyword' } }];\n}\n\nlet statsBlock = '';\nlet sourceCount = 0;\nlet errorMsg = null;\n\ntry {\n  // 1. Exa search\n  const exaResp = await this.helpers.httpRequest({\n    method: 'POST',\n    url: 'https://api.exa.ai/search',\n    headers: {\n      'x-api-key': EXA_API_KEY,\n      'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n    },\n    body: {\n      query: query + ' statistics data study research',\n      numResults: 8,\n      type: 'neural',\n      useAutoprompt: true\n    },\n    json: true,\n    timeout: 30000\n  });\n\n  if (!exaResp || !Array.isArray(exaResp.results) || exaResp.results.length === 0) {\n    errorMsg = 'No statistical sources found';\n  } else {\n    // 2. Fetch contents\n    const ids = exaResp.results.slice(0, 8).map(r => r.id).filter(Boolean);\n    const contentsResp = await this.helpers.httpRequest({\n      method: 'POST',\n      url: 'https://api.exa.ai/contents',\n      headers: {\n        'x-api-key': EXA_API_KEY,\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n      },\n      body: {\n        ids,\n        text: { maxCharacters: 4000, includeHtmlTags: false }\n      },\n      json: true,\n      timeout: 30000\n    });\n\n    const textById = new Map();\n    if (contentsResp && Array.isArray(contentsResp.results)) {\n      for (const c of contentsResp.results) {\n        if (c.id && c.text) textById.set(c.id, c.text);\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Collect meaningful texts\n    const texts = [];\n    for (const r of exaResp.results) {\n      const body = (textById.get(r.id) || '').trim();\n      if (body.length > 100) {\n        texts.push('[Source: ' + (r.title || r.url || 'unknown') + ']\\n' + body);\n        sourceCount++;\n      }\n      if (sourceCount >= 5) break;\n    }\n\n    if (texts.length === 0) {\n      errorMsg = 'Exa results had insufficient text content';\n    } else {\n      // 3. Summarise with Gemini Flash\n      const combined = texts.join('\\n\\n---\\n\\n');\n      const llmResp = await this.helpers.httpRequest({\n        method: 'POST',\n        url: 'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions',\n        headers: {\n          'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + OPENROUTER_API_KEY,\n          'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n          'HTTP-Referer': 'https://shettymarketing.com',\n          'X-Title': 'Blog Post Creator (n8n)'\n        },\n        body: {\n          model: STATS_MODEL,\n          messages: [\n            { role: 'system', content: 'You are a research assistant. Extract relevant statistics, data points, percentages, study findings, and research results from the provided sources. Output a concise bullet-point list. Include the specific numbers and cite the source name in brackets. Format: \"- [statistic] [source name]\". If a source has no concrete data, skip it. Output only the bullet list, no preamble.' },\n            { role: 'user', content: 'Extract all statistics, data points, and research findings from the following sources about \"' + query + '\". Return only the bullet-point list:\\n\\n' + combined }\n          ],\n          temperature: 0\n        },\n        json: true,\n        timeout: 60000\n      });\n\n      statsBlock = llmResp?.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || '';\n    }\n  }\n} catch (err) {\n  errorMsg = 'Stats scraping failed: ' + (err.message || String(err));\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    stats_enabled: true,\n    stats_block: statsBlock,\n    source_count: sourceCount,\n    error: errorMsg\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "outline-stats",
      "name": "Stats Scrape",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        120,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Build the OpenRouter request body for blog-post outline generation.\n//\n// REPLACE the OPENROUTER_API_KEY constant and tune OUTLINE_MODEL below.\n\nconst OPENROUTER_API_KEY = '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';\nconst OUTLINE_MODEL      = 'google/gemini-2.5-flash';\n\nconst form = $('Fetch Writing Style (Outline)').first().json;\nconst stats = $('Stats Scrape').first().json;\nconst empathy = $('Empathy Research').first().json;\n\n// Word count breakdown calculation\nconst targetWC = form.target_word_count || 0;\nlet wcBreakdown = '';\n\nif (targetWC > 0) {\n  const introWords = Math.round(targetWC * 0.10);\n  const conclusionWords = Math.round(targetWC * 0.10);\n  const bodyWords = targetWC - introWords - conclusionWords;\n  const estimatedH2 = 5;\n  const wordsPerH2 = Math.round(bodyWords / estimatedH2);\n  \n  wcBreakdown = '\\n\\nWORD COUNT TARGET: ' + targetWC + ' words (\\u00b15% tolerance: ' + Math.round(targetWC * 0.95) + '-' + Math.round(targetWC * 1.05) + ' words)\\n- Intro paragraph: ~' + introWords + ' words (above-the-fold, before first H2)\\n- Each H2 section: ~' + wordsPerH2 + ' words (' + estimatedH2 + ' sections)\\n- Conclusion: ~' + conclusionWords + ' words\\n\\nThe outline MUST have enough H2/H3 depth to support this word count. Each section description should include its target word count.';\n}\n\nconst systemPrompt = 'You are a senior blog editor and SEO strategist. You write blog-post outlines that rank in Google AND are quoted by LLM-based search (ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity).\\n\\n' +\n'GROUNDING RULES (ordered by priority):\\n' +\n'1. SEARCH INTENT INSIGHTS (HIGHEST PRIORITY): If <intent_context> contains content, treat it as authoritative truth about what users searching this topic actually want. Shape the outline to address the stated primary intent. Use sub-intents to inspire section topics. If a recommended page archetype is specified (listicle, guide, how-to, comparison, etc.), you MUST follow it exactly. Do NOT default to a generic guide structure if the intent calls for a listicle. If a modifier-SERP conflict is flagged, follow that guidance.\\n' +\n'2. SERP ANALYSIS (HIGHEST PRIORITY): If <serp_context> contains content, use it as authoritative competitive intelligence. Follow the SERP archetype specified. Match common patterns across top rankers. Incorporate standout signals as differentiators. Implement recommendations as structural requirements. This carries the same weight as Search Intent Insights.\\n' +\n'3. SALIENCE INSIGHTS (SECOND HIGHEST PRIORITY): If <salience_context> contains content (must-cover entities, H2 candidates, supporting topics), weave must-cover entities using exact entity names. Use H2/H3 candidates from salience as structural anchors. Give must-cover entities their own H2/H3 if they are significant enough.\\n' +\n'4. Design the blog structure yourself. Choose the best H1 title, section headings, and flow based on the topic, voice, anecdotes, opinions, stats, and keyword context provided. Do NOT follow a fixed template -- let the content dictate the structure.\\n' +\n'5. The H1 must include the Focus Keyword naturally. It should read like a compelling blog title, not a keyword-stuffed headline.\\n' +\n'6. Every section body must be one or two short lines describing what the writer should cover in that section, citing which keywords / entities / anecdotes / stats to weave in. Do NOT write the actual paragraph content here -- outlines only.\\n' +\n'7. Weave keywords naturally: Focus Keyword in the H1 and intro, Header Keywords in H2/H3 headings, Entities where they add authority, Common/Extra Keywords throughout body descriptions.\\n' +\n'8. If <voice_context> is provided, write all section descriptions in that exact voice -- mirror the tone, style, perspective, and audience level described.\\n' +\n'9. If <anecdotes> are provided, place each anecdote in the most relevant section -- tag it as [Include anecdote: <summary>] in the section body.\\n' +\n'10. If <opinions> are provided, ensure at least 1-2 sections explicitly call out the unique/contrarian takes. Tag them as [POV: <summary>].\\n' +\n'11. If <stats_context> is provided (statistics and data points from live research), weave the most relevant stats into appropriate sections. Tag them as [Include stat: <summary>]. Do not fabricate new stats.\\n' +\n'12. AUDIENCE RESEARCH: If <audience_context> contains content (problem clusters with questions and content angles), use the user problems as primary inspiration for section topics. Address the top emotional/practical concerns early, not buried deep.\\n' +\n'13. EMPATHY INSIGHTS: If <empathy_context> contains content (reader pain points, objections, problems, fears from real communities), use these to shape section topics and angles. Address top pain points early in the post. Frame objections as things to overcome. Mirror the reader\\'s own language from quotes. Dedicate sections to the highest-weight themes.\\n' +\nwcBreakdown + '\\n\\n' +\n'TONE: Match the provided voice exactly. If no voice is provided, default to conversational, authoritative, and benefit-driven.\\n\\n' +\n'OUTPUT: Plain markdown. No preamble. No trailing commentary. No code fences.';\n\nconst parts = [];\n// PRIORITY ORDER: intent > serp > salience > keywords > anecdotes/opinions > rest\nparts.push('<intent_context>\\n' + (form.intent_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</intent_context>');\nparts.push('<serp_context>\\n' + (form.serp_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</serp_context>');\nparts.push('<salience_context>\\n' + (form.salience_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</salience_context>');\nparts.push('<marketer_inputs>\\nFocus Keyword: ' + (form.focus_keyword || '(not set)') + '\\nHeader Keywords: ' + ((form.header_keywords || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + '\\nEntities: ' + ((form.entities || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + '\\nCommon Keywords: ' + ((form.common_keywords || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + '\\nExtra Keywords: ' + ((form.extra_keywords || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + (targetWC > 0 ? '\\nTarget Word Count: ' + targetWC + ' words' : '') + '\\n</marketer_inputs>');\nif (form.anecdotes) parts.push('<anecdotes>\\n' + form.anecdotes + '\\n</anecdotes>');\nif (form.opinions) parts.push('<opinions>\\n' + form.opinions + '\\n</opinions>');\nparts.push('<topic>\\n' + (form.topic || form.focus_keyword || '(not set)') + '\\n</topic>');\nif (form.voice) parts.push('<voice_context>\\n' + form.voice + '\\n</voice_context>');\nif (stats.stats_block) parts.push('<stats_context>\\n' + stats.stats_block + '\\n</stats_context>');\nif (empathy.empathy_block) parts.push('<empathy_context>\\n' + empathy.empathy_block + '\\n</empathy_context>');\nparts.push('<audience_context>\\n' + (form.audience_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</audience_context>');\nparts.push('Now produce the blog-post outline.');\nconst userPrompt = parts.join('\\n\\n');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    form,\n    stats,\n    empathy,\n    outline_model: OUTLINE_MODEL,\n    openrouter_api_key: OPENROUTER_API_KEY,\n    openrouter_request: {\n      model: OUTLINE_MODEL,\n      messages: [\n        { role: 'system', content: systemPrompt },\n        { role: 'user', content: userPrompt }\n      ],\n      temperature: 0.3,\n      max_tokens: 8192\n    }\n  }\n}];\n"
      },
      "id": "outline-build-prompt",
      "name": "Build Outline Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        340,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $json.openrouter_api_key }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            },
            {
              "name": "HTTP-Referer",
              "value": "https://shettymarketing.com"
            },
            {
              "name": "X-Title",
              "value": "Blog Post Creator (n8n)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.openrouter_request) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 120000
        }
      },
      "id": "outline-openrouter",
      "name": "OpenRouter (Outline)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        560,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Extract the markdown outline from the OpenRouter response.\nconst resp = $input.first().json;\nconst payload = $('Build Outline Prompt').first().json;\n\nif (resp.error) {\n  return [{ json: { error: 'OpenRouter returned error', detail: resp.error } }];\n}\n\nconst choice = resp?.choices?.[0];\n\n// Check for upstream timeout (504) — content is null but reasoning exists\nif (!choice?.message?.content && choice?.error?.code === 504) {\n  return [{ json: { \n    error: 'Model timed out (504). Please try again.', \n    retry: true,\n    detail: choice.error.message || 'Upstream idle timeout exceeded'\n  }}];\n}\n\nconst outline = choice?.message?.content;\nif (!outline) {\n  return [{ json: { error: 'No outline in OpenRouter response', raw: resp } }];\n}\n\nconst cleaned = outline.replace(/```(?:markdown|md)?\\s*/i, '').replace(/\\s*```\\s*$/i, '').trim();\n\nconst result = {\n  request: {\n    topic: payload.form?.topic,\n    focus_keyword: payload.form?.focus_keyword,\n    header_keywords: payload.form?.header_keywords,\n    entities: payload.form?.entities,\n    common_keywords: payload.form?.common_keywords,\n    extra_keywords: payload.form?.extra_keywords,\n    target_word_count: payload.form?.target_word_count\n  },\n  outline: cleaned,\n  model: payload.outline_model,\n  usage: resp.usage || null,\n  generated_at: new Date().toISOString()\n};\n\nif (payload.stats && payload.stats.stats_enabled) {\n  result.stats = {\n    enabled: true,\n    source_count: payload.stats.source_count,\n    stats_block: payload.stats.stats_block,\n    error: payload.stats.error || null\n  };\n}\n\nif (payload.empathy && payload.empathy.empathy_enabled) {\n  result.empathy = {\n    enabled: true,\n    source_count: payload.empathy.source_count,\n    empathy_block: payload.empathy.empathy_block,\n    error: payload.empathy.error || null\n  };\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: result }];"
      },
      "id": "outline-parse",
      "name": "Parse Outline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        780,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "outline-respond",
      "name": "Respond with Outline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1000,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "blog-post-content",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {
          "allowedOrigins": "*"
        }
      },
      "id": "content-webhook",
      "name": "Content Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -500,
        600
      ],
      "webhookId": "blog-post-content"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "is-test-cond-content",
              "leftValue": "={{ !!($json.body?.test || $json.test) }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "content-is-test",
      "name": "Is Content Test?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -300,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { \"ok\": true, \"message\": \"Webhook reachable\", \"received_at\": $now.toISO() } }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "content-respond-test",
      "name": "Respond Content Test OK",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -100,
        400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Normalize inputs for the blog-post-content webhook.\nconst input = $input.first().json;\nconst form = (input && typeof input.body === 'object' && input.body !== null && Object.keys(input.body).length > 0)\n  ? input.body\n  : input;\n\nconst norm = s => String(s).toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '');\nconst pick = (...keys) => {\n  for (const k of keys) {\n    if (form[k] !== undefined && form[k] !== null && form[k] !== '') return form[k];\n  }\n  const targets = keys.map(norm);\n  for (const k of Object.keys(form)) {\n    const n = norm(k);\n    if (targets.some(t => n === t || n.startsWith(t))) return form[k];\n  }\n  return '';\n};\n\nconst toArr = v => {\n  if (Array.isArray(v)) return v.map(x => String(x).trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  if (typeof v === 'string') return v.split(/[,;\\n]/).map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n  return [];\n};\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    edited_outline: pick('edited_outline', 'outline', 'editedOutline') || '',\n    focus_keyword: pick('focus_keyword', 'Focus Keyword', 'focusKeyword') || '',\n    header_keywords: toArr(pick('header_keywords', 'Header Keywords', 'headerKeywords')),\n    entities: toArr(pick('entities', 'Entities')),\n    common_keywords: toArr(pick('common_keywords', 'Common Keywords', 'commonKeywords')),\n    extra_keywords: toArr(pick('extra_keywords', 'Extra Keywords', 'extraKeywords')),\n    target_word_count: parseInt(pick('target_word_count', 'Target Word Count', 'targetWordCount')) || 0,\n    intent_context_text: String(pick('intent_context_text', 'intentContextText') || '').trim(),\n    serp_context_text: String(pick('serp_context_text', 'serpContextText') || '').trim(),\n    salience_context_text: String(pick('salience_context_text', 'salienceContextText') || '').trim(),\n    audience_context_text: String(pick('audience_context_text', 'audienceContextText') || '').trim()\n  }\n}];\n"
      },
      "id": "content-normalize",
      "name": "Normalize Content Inputs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -100,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Build the OpenRouter request body for final blog content generation from the edited outline.\n//\n// REPLACE the OPENROUTER_API_KEY constant and tune CONTENT_MODEL below.\n\nconst OPENROUTER_API_KEY = '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';\nconst CONTENT_MODEL      = 'google/gemini-2.5-pro';\n\nconst form = $('Fetch Writing Style (Content)').first().json;\n\nif (!form.edited_outline) {\n  return [{ json: { error: 'edited_outline is required' } }];\n}\n\n// Word count enforcement calculation\nconst targetWC = form.target_word_count || 0;\nlet wcEnforcement = '';\n\nif (targetWC > 0) {\n  const h2Matches = (form.edited_outline || '').match(/^##\\s+/gm) || [];\n  const h2Count = Math.max(h2Matches.length, 1);\n  const introWords = Math.round(targetWC * 0.10);\n  const conclusionWords = Math.round(targetWC * 0.10);\n  const bodyWords = targetWC - introWords - conclusionWords;\n  const wordsPerH2 = Math.round(bodyWords / h2Count);\n  \n  wcEnforcement = '\\n\\nWORD COUNT ENFORCEMENT (NON-NEGOTIABLE):\\n- TOTAL: ' + targetWC + ' words (\\u00b15% tolerance: ' + Math.round(targetWC * 0.95) + '-' + Math.round(targetWC * 1.05) + ' words)\\n- Intro paragraph: ' + introWords + ' words exactly\\n- Each H2 section: ' + wordsPerH2 + ' words exactly (' + h2Count + ' sections)\\n- Conclusion: ' + conclusionWords + ' words exactly\\n\\nRULES:\\n1. Count words as you write each section\\n2. Hit the target for EACH section, not just the total\\n3. If a section is short, expand with examples, data, or explanations\\n4. If a section is long, tighten prose without losing meaning\\n5. Do NOT add filler to hit counts - every word must add value\\n6. The final output MUST be within \\u00b15% of ' + targetWC + ' words';\n}\n\nconst systemPrompt = (form.writing_style_instructions ? '\\n\\nCRITICAL WRITING STYLE RULES (MANDATORY \\u2014 follow EVERY rule below exactly. These OVERRIDE all other tone/style guidance):\\n' + form.writing_style_instructions + '\\n\\n---\\n\\nThe CRITICAL rules above are your HIGHEST priority. Every sentence you write MUST comply with them. Now follow the additional SEO/structure rules below:\\n\\n' : '') +\n'You are a senior blog editor and SEO copywriter. You write blog-post content that ranks in Google AND is quoted by LLM-based search.\\n\\n' +\n'GROUNDING RULES (ordered by priority):\\n' +\n'1. SEARCH INTENT INSIGHTS (HIGHEST PRIORITY): If <intent_context> contains content, calibrate tone, depth, and CTAs to the stated primary intent. Transactional -> buy/subscribe CTAs. Informational -> no heavy sell, focus on teaching. If a recommended page archetype is specified (listicle, guide, how-to, comparison), you MUST follow that archetype. If a modifier-SERP conflict is flagged, follow that guidance.\\n' +\n'2. SERP ANALYSIS (HIGHEST PRIORITY): If <serp_context> contains content, use it as authoritative competitive intelligence. Follow the SERP archetype specified. Match common patterns across top rankers. Incorporate standout signals as differentiators. Implement recommendations as content improvements. This carries the same weight as Search Intent Insights.\\n' +\n'3. SALIENCE INSIGHTS (SECOND HIGHEST PRIORITY): If <salience_context> contains content, weave must-cover entities naturally throughout the body copy using exact entity names.\\n' +\n'4. Expand every section of the provided outline into final blog copy. Do NOT add, remove, or reorder sections unless the outline explicitly signals flexibility.\\n' +\n'5. Under every heading, write engaging, authentic prose. H2s get 2-4 paragraphs. H3s get 1-2 paragraphs. The intro hook should grab attention in the first sentence -- use a stat, a provocative statement, or a vivid anecdote as appropriate.\\n' +\n'6. Naturally weave in the Focus Keyword, Header Keywords, Entities, and Common Keywords. Use the Focus Keyword in the H1 and once in the opening paragraph. Use Entities where they add trust signals. Do not keyword-stuff.\\n' +\n'7. If the outline contains [Include anecdote: ...] tags, expand the anecdote into full narrative prose in that section. Make it personal and vivid.\\n' +\n'8. If the outline contains [POV: ...] tags, expand the opinion into a clear, confident position statement with supporting reasoning.\\n' +\n'9. If the outline contains [Include stat: ...] tags, present the statistic naturally with proper attribution -- \"According to [source], ...\" or similar phrasing. Do not fabricate stats not present in the outline tags.\\n' +\n'10. If <voice_context> was provided, the entire post must read in that voice -- every sentence, every transition, every takeaway. The voice is non-negotiable.\\n' +\n'11. For any [TO FILL] markers in the outline, leave a [TO FILL: <label>] placeholder instead of fabricating.\\n' +\n'12. AUDIENCE RESEARCH: If <audience_context> contains content, address the top user problems explicitly. Use the phrasing patterns from representative questions to write relatable copy.\\n' +\n'13. PARAGRAPH LENGTH (NON-NEGOTIABLE): Every paragraph must be a MINIMUM of 3 lines and a MAXIMUM of 4 lines. This is critical for readability -- large chunks of text ruin the reading experience. If a paragraph runs longer than 4 lines, break it into two paragraphs. If a paragraph is shorter than 3 lines, expand it with supporting detail or merge it with an adjacent paragraph.' +\nwcEnforcement + '\\n\\n' +\n'FORMAT: Pure markdown. Preserve H1/H2/H3 structure exactly. No preamble, no trailing commentary, no code fences.\\n\\n' +\n'TONE: Match the provided voice exactly. If no voice provided, default to conversational, authoritative, and benefit-driven. Short sentences. No filler phrases. No fluff.' +\n(form.writing_style_instructions ? '\\n\\nWRITING STYLE INSTRUCTIONS (follow these precisely):\\n' + form.writing_style_instructions : '');\n\nconst parts = [];\n// PRIORITY ORDER: intent > serp > salience > keywords > anecdotes/opinions > audience > outline\nparts.push('<intent_context>\\n' + (form.intent_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</intent_context>');\nparts.push('<serp_context>\\n' + (form.serp_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</serp_context>');\nparts.push('<salience_context>\\n' + (form.salience_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</salience_context>');\nparts.push('<marketer_inputs>\\nFocus Keyword: ' + (form.focus_keyword || '(not set)') + '\\nHeader Keywords: ' + ((form.header_keywords || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + '\\nEntities: ' + ((form.entities || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + '\\nCommon Keywords: ' + ((form.common_keywords || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + '\\nExtra Keywords: ' + ((form.extra_keywords || []).join(', ') || '(not set)') + (targetWC > 0 ? '\\nTarget Word Count: ' + targetWC + ' words' : '') + '\\n</marketer_inputs>');\n// Anecdotes & Opinions reinforcement -- remind the AI of raw material even though outline tags carry them too\nif (form.anecdotes || form.opinions) {\n  let reinforce = '';\n  if (form.anecdotes) reinforce += 'Anecdotes to incorporate:\\n' + form.anecdotes;\n  if (form.opinions) reinforce += (reinforce ? '\\n\\n' : '') + 'Opinions to weave in:\\n' + form.opinions;\n  parts.push('<anecdotes_opinions>\\n' + reinforce + '\\n</anecdotes_opinions>');\n}\nparts.push('<audience_context>\\n' + (form.audience_context_text || '(not provided)') + '\\n</audience_context>');\nparts.push('<edited_outline>\\n' + form.edited_outline + '\\n</edited_outline>');\nparts.push((targetWC > 0 ? 'CRITICAL: You MUST write exactly ' + targetWC + ' words (\\u00b15% tolerance). Count words as you write. Each section MUST hit its word count target.\\n\\n' : '') + 'Now expand the outline into final blog-post content.');\nconst userPrompt = parts.join('\\n\\n');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    form,\n    content_model: CONTENT_MODEL,\n    openrouter_api_key: OPENROUTER_API_KEY,\n    openrouter_request: {\n      model: CONTENT_MODEL,\n      messages: [\n        { role: 'system', content: systemPrompt },\n        { role: 'user', content: userPrompt }\n      ],\n      temperature: 0.35,\n      max_tokens: 16384\n    }\n  }\n}];\n"
      },
      "id": "content-build-prompt",
      "name": "Build Content Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        120,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $json.openrouter_api_key }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            },
            {
              "name": "HTTP-Referer",
              "value": "https://shettymarketing.com"
            },
            {
              "name": "X-Title",
              "value": "Blog Post Creator (n8n)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.openrouter_request) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 120000
        }
      },
      "id": "content-openrouter",
      "name": "OpenRouter (Content)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        340,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Extract the final markdown content from the OpenRouter response.\nconst resp = $input.first().json;\nconst payload = $('Build Content Prompt').first().json;\n\nif (payload.error) {\n  return [{ json: payload }];\n}\n\nif (resp.error) {\n  return [{ json: { error: 'OpenRouter returned error', detail: resp.error } }];\n}\n\nconst content = resp?.choices?.[0]?.message?.content;\nif (!content) {\n  return [{ json: { error: 'No content in OpenRouter response', raw: resp } }];\n}\n\nconst cleaned = content.replace(/^```(?:markdown|md)?\\s*/i, '').replace(/\\s*```\\s*$/i, '').trim();\n\nconst wordCount = cleaned.split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;\nconst h1Count = (cleaned.match(/^#\\s+/gm) || []).length;\nconst h2Count = (cleaned.match(/^##\\s+/gm) || []).length;\nconst h3Count = (cleaned.match(/^###\\s+/gm) || []).length;\n\n// Word count validation\nconst targetWC = payload.form?.target_word_count || 0;\nlet wordCountStatus = 'no_target';\nlet wordCountDeviation = 0;\nlet wordCountTolerance = { min: 0, max: 0 };\n\nif (targetWC > 0) {\n  wordCountTolerance = {\n    min: Math.round(targetWC * 0.95),\n    max: Math.round(targetWC * 1.05)\n  };\n  wordCountDeviation = Math.round(((wordCount - targetWC) / targetWC) * 100);\n  \n  if (wordCount >= wordCountTolerance.min && wordCount <= wordCountTolerance.max) {\n    wordCountStatus = 'on_target';\n  } else if (wordCount > wordCountTolerance.max) {\n    wordCountStatus = 'over_target';\n  } else {\n    wordCountStatus = 'under_target';\n  }\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    request: {\n      focus_keyword: payload.form?.focus_keyword,\n      header_keywords: payload.form?.header_keywords,\n      entities: payload.form?.entities,\n      common_keywords: payload.form?.common_keywords,\n      extra_keywords: payload.form?.extra_keywords,\n      target_word_count: targetWC\n    },\n    content: cleaned,\n    model: payload.content_model,\n    stats: { \n      word_count: wordCount, \n      target_word_count: targetWC,\n      word_count_deviation: wordCountDeviation + '%',\n      word_count_status: wordCountStatus,\n      word_count_tolerance: wordCountTolerance,\n      h1: h1Count, \n      h2: h2Count, \n      h3: h3Count \n    },\n    usage: resp.usage || null,\n    generated_at: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "content-parse",
      "name": "Parse Content",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        560,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Humanize the generated content via external Humanizer API.\n// If humanize_enabled is false or humanize_webhook is empty, pass through unchanged.\nconst input = $input.first().json;\nconst humanizeEnabled = input.humanize_enabled !== false;\nconst humanizeWebhook = (input.humanize_webhook || '').trim();\n\nif (!humanizeEnabled || !humanizeWebhook) {\n  return [{ json: input }];\n}\n\nconst content = input.content || '';\nif (!content.trim()) {\n  return [{ json: input }];\n}\n\ntry {\n  const resp = await this.helpers.httpRequest({\n    method: 'POST',\n    url: humanizeWebhook,\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: {\n      text: content,\n      p_syn: 0.2,\n      p_trans: 0.2,\n      preserve_linebreaks: true\n    },\n    json: true,\n    timeout: 120000\n  });\n\n  if (resp && resp.humanized_text) {\n    return [{\n      json: {\n        ...input,\n        content: resp.humanized_text,\n        humanize_stats: {\n          words_added: resp.words_added || 0,\n          sentences_added: resp.sentences_added || 0,\n          orig_word_count: resp.orig_word_count || 0,\n          new_word_count: resp.new_word_count || 0\n        }\n      }\n    }];\n  }\n} catch (err) {\n  // If humanizer fails, return original content with error note\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: input }];"
      },
      "id": "content-humanize",
      "name": "Humanize Content",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        670,
        600
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
